Q: Fill Stripe Elements Card with Playwright A: <p>The answers here guided me in the right direction, but unfortunately they don't work in 2026 (at least when trying with multiple payment methods like card + iDEAL). I did this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>clickChooseCreditCardButton = async () =&gt; {
    await this.payWithCardButton.evaluate((el: HTMLElement) =&gt; el.click()); 
}

fillData = async (email: string, cardNumber: string, expiryDate: string, cvc: string, name: string) =&gt; {
    await this.emailInput.fill(email);
    await this.cardNumberInput.click();
    await this.cardNumberInput.fill(cardNumber);
    await this.expiryDateInput.fill(expiryDate);
    await this.cvcInput.fill(cvc);
    await this.holderNameInput.fill(name);
}

constructor(page: Page) {
    this.page = page;
    this.cardNumberInput = this.page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Card number' });
    this.expiryDateInput = this.page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Expiration' });
    this.cvcInput = this.page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'CVC' });
}
</code></pre>
<p>And then, in the test:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const stripeCheckoutPage = new StripeCheckoutPage(page);
await stripeCheckoutPage.clickChooseCreditCardButton();
await stripeCheckoutPage.fillData('john.doe@example.com', '4242424242424242', '1249', '123', 'John Doe');

</code></pre>
<p>It is important to note that this will only work if the Stripe UI language is set to English. If you need to manage other languages you must find the correct selectors. It's a bit flaky but of course Stripe does not want people using Playwright to automate payments, so these are expected to break.</p>
